# Line endings are NORMALISED TO LF in the repository, and checked out as LF everywhere.
#
# This is not a style preference; two gates depend on it:
#
#   1. The commit guards and test harnesses are bash scripts. A .sh file checked out with CRLF
#      fails on Linux and macOS with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" - so a Windows clone would
#      publish guards that cannot run for anyone else.
#
#   2. scripts/theme-build.mjs --check compares the generated theme files BYTE FOR BYTE against
#      freshly generated content, which always uses \n. If git handed those files back with CRLF
#      on checkout, gate G1 would report DRIFT on a clean tree, on every Windows machine, forever.
#      (The same class of defect as the Windows path separators fixed in v1.2.0.)
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by normalisation.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
